y-id "q-35318" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35318/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35318"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "13b5bace-ecf9-54fd-a0b5-f9dcfd214b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ba715dfb-63d8-57d8-98eb-d748539e0f28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6b1647ae-9b3d-567b-8ee0-590a76a8603c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e5baea4f-9bc6-54b4-bdbd-539478c7752b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "46493b1a-d566-5974-a5b2-6cc33865f1b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93e26811-707c-542a-8c14-6dafeed2bd49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35348/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-35348/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-35348/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-35348/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-35348/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-35348/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35348" :question/id #uuid "daab19d5-bf99-519c-b857-bce1128afeef" :question/math-academy-id "q-35348" :question/problem "Given $Z=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))$, we reduce $Z$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+(-\\frac{2}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-35348/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35348"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35349"] :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $4$th columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1+2+0=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "8d83f58a-e8e5-593b-af7f-cf926bdab03d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "528d1861-3336-579a-a6af-82d402e095ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "b1ed8aa0-75d2-5f74-8203-9a155629e396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "bef5420b-2662-5de7-99c4-43398761f3d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "dba79471-ee02-58ef-b2fd-1abe42bc188d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4005ef44-3477-5cb7-a13b-40fda2dc0064" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79336/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-79336/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-79336/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-79336/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-79336/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-79336/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79336" :question/id #uuid "585570f5-8f9c-5c98-a1b7-b1b44c87b365" :question/math-academy-id "q-79336" :question/problem "Let $Q$ be a $5\\times 8$ matrix that has $5$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $Q?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(Q))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $Q.$ \n\nSince $Q$ has $8$ columns and $5$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $Q$ is \n\n$$\n8-5=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(Q))=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79336/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79336"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "932d5dea-43c5-5d7d-95f4-0e4f9b8b9d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "624e1d0c-cd74-5e91-8efa-53087a853596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ec436cc7-7876-57a0-a969-10f75ef6a459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "115bdaee-f46e-50df-8c5d-006013b38843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "102591f6-0608-55e9-8c95-169cd337ad4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be8be31f-e4ef-525c-80ff-4091d9770d58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139974/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-139974/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-139974/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-139974/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-139974/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-139974/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139974" :question/id #uuid "865fdfe5-f0b6-527a-b037-58ab9657cb54" :question/math-academy-id "q-139974" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd  column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2+1+1=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-139974/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
